Title: Diogo Jota: Liverpool pay tribute to forward in first match since his death
Date: 2025-07-13
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Liverpool fan Jane', 'Text': '"I feel very emotional," Liverpool fan Jane, wearing a custom T-shirt dedicated to Jota, said. "I feel very proud of my team and all the tributes they\'ve put together."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 20, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 134}}, {'Speaker': 'Mathew', 'Text': '"It has been really difficult," he said. "I told my seven-year-old on the morning it happened and he just burst into tears. It\'s very hard for him to understand."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 21, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 156}}, {'Speaker': 'Rafael', 'Text': 'Mathew\'s 15-year-old son Rafael – named after Champions League-winning Liverpool manager Rafael Benitez - added: "I feel gutted. But Liverpool is a family and we\'ve all come together to pay our respects in the right way."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 22, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 178}}, {'Speaker': 'Arne Slot', 'Text': 'In his first interview since Jota\'s death, Liverpool head coach Arne Slot told Liverpool TV: "If we want to laugh, we laugh; if we want to cry, we\'re going to cry.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 13, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 155}}, {'Speaker': 'Arne Slot', 'Text': '"If they want to train they can train, if they don\'t want to train they can not train. But be yourself, don\'t think you have to be different than your emotions tell you.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 14, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 136}}, {'Speaker': 'Arne Slot', 'Text': '"We will always carry him with us in our hearts, in our thoughts, wherever we go."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 15, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 69}}], 'Description': [{'Description': 'During the latter, a visibly emotional Preston captain Ben Whiteman laid a wreath in front of the travelling Liverpool supporters.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 108}}, {'Description': "The away end, filled with flags and scarves commemorating the former Porto and Wolves attacker, loudly sang Jota's song as the players walked out before an impeccably observed minute's silence.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 164}}, {'Description': "At the start of the 20th minute, the crowd burst into another rendition of Jota's song.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 70}}, {'Description': 'There was a muted celebration when Conor Bradley opened the scoring for Liverpool, with the full-back looking up to the heavens as he walked back to his position.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 7, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 146}}, {'Description': "Striker Darwin Nunez scored the Reds' second and paid his own tribute by doing two of Jota's celebrations in front of the Liverpool fans.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 8, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 117}}, {'Description': "Cody Gakpo followed suit after adding the third in a 3-1 win and then held his fingers up to signal the number 20, Jota's squad number at Liverpool.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 9, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 131}}, {'Description': 'The match programme had a black and white picture of Jota holding the Premier League trophy and featured tributes to the Liverpool player and his brother.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 10, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 129}}, {'Description': "Liverpool have retired Jota's number 20 shirt across all areas of the club, making the announcement at 20:20 BST on Friday.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 11, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 112}}, {'Description': 'Thousands of Liverpool fans travelled to Deepdale, in practice to watch their team undertake their first run-out of the new campaign, but in reality to pay tribute to Jota and Silva and to show support to the team and coaching staff.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 17, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 207}}, {'Description': "Those who packed out the Bill Shankly Kop belted out Jota's name before kick-off and followed that up with regular airing throughout the match, with Preston supporters joining them, standing and clapping along in rhythm, for a rendition in the 20th minute.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 18, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 212}}, {'Description': 'The way in which it was bellowed this afternoon conveyed an immense depth of feeling for a footballer adored by followers of his club, while for those on the pitch, playing without him for the first time will have been just one of many important stages of their grief.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 24, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 219}}, {'Description': 'There have scarcely been football matches less important than this, and yet, very few which have been imbued with as much meaning, emotion, and sheer love by those who made sure they were there to play their part.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 25, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 186}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': "Liverpool players observe a minute's silence for Diogo Jota and Andre Silva ahead of friendly match at Preston"}]}
